  "id": "tympanic-membrane",
  "term": "tympanic membrane",
  "definition": "The tympanic membrane is a thin membrane that separates the outer ear canal from the middle ear. It moves with air pressure changes in the outer ear and helps pass sound energy along by making the small ear bones vibrate.",
